                                "example_id": "de62a02d-fdb4-4376-8171-bf26bd7931d1",
                                "sense_id": "22d81ac0-4801-3188-b0ca-9acf9d349218",
                                "text": "Chemins impratiqués."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fdf82b48-a7e9-49ac-8b28-746edbb7ab11",
                        "source_entry_id": "6f268afb-0fd3-3052-b9ee-f6ff8c93a41b",
                        "source_sense_id": "22d81ac0-4801-3188-b0ca-9acf9d349218",
                        "target_lang_word": "untrodden",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "untrodden",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd982a5b-3506-3747-a22f-7aede24ac3e1",
                                        "entry_id": "3d559823-66d1-30a9-a036-ad03a51310eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That has never been trod upon; unexplored, unspoiled."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2a99e746-5ad7-483a-b68b-19aee09e6f81",
                                                "sense_id": "bd982a5b-3506-3747-a22f-7aede24ac3e1",
                                                "text": "Proofs of the presence of the white man are found all over the Territory in the shape of old bouilli tins, &c., and often when out after a strayed horse, I have imagined myself to be in wilds untrodden except by the foot of the blackfellow, but the sight of an unassuming empty sardine tin would remind me that the ubiquitous digger had been there first."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca7abc5e-cda5-49ec-931a-9d99b7e89877",
                                                "sense_id": "bd982a5b-3506-3747-a22f-7aede24ac3e1",
                                                "text": "If he could only get away from the holes in the banks, he thought, there would be no more faces. He swung off the path and plunged into the untrodden places of the wood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2fd6abd-2f2e-42ef-b730-a1d21a47d4e8",
                                                "sense_id": "bd982a5b-3506-3747-a22f-7aede24ac3e1",
                                                "text": "Their path led them past sharp cliffs, along narrow trails unknown and untrodden, past headlong boulders strewn across barren, treeless, wind-haunted heights."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f321baa4-fdd0-4fdc-97e7-501a812a53cb",
                                                "sense_id": "bd982a5b-3506-3747-a22f-7aede24ac3e1",
                                                "text": "Moreover the most becoming place for temples and altars he said to be that which, while being most visible, would be most untrodden; for it is pleasant for those who are undefiled to approach it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0fbbf266-0cc3-4bd8-b281-962f52869793",
                                                "sense_id": "bd982a5b-3506-3747-a22f-7aede24ac3e1",
                                                "text": "The upper layer of the soil is, therefore, less solid than in other trampled habitats and the optimum development of the community can only take place in the broader joints between paving stones in more untrodden places, often in strips of pavement at the foots^([sic]) of walls where the shifting sand accumulates and turbulent air currents may play an important role."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b9271ee9-ae6a-3f9f-b967-a2ff879611f6",
                                        "entry_id": "3d559823-66d1-30a9-a036-ad03a51310eb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a person: undefeated."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "adb2a084-e3e9-4adf-8fab-a0286fea1c75",
                        "source_entry_id": "6f268afb-0fd3-3052-b9ee-f6ff8c93a41b",
                        "source_sense_id": "22d81ac0-4801-3188-b0ca-9acf9d349218",
                        "target_lang_word": "trackless",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "trackless",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e6b7055-2cb3-3ce7-8ed4-a1636b8a703c",
                                        "entry_id": "0119e4ed-481a-3b0f-83f4-1d6d11edc4ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a place: not having tracks or paths; pathless, untrodden; also, having had all tracks removed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8bb7b995-61d2-426c-a3e5-060670cbc3bd",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6b7055-2cb3-3ce7-8ed4-a1636b8a703c",
                                                "text": "a trackless desert    a trackless forest"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "33c874f5-8e60-4e3b-b1ad-bc8bb423e615",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6b7055-2cb3-3ce7-8ed4-a1636b8a703c",
                                                "text": "Associates! Solitude in trackless deserts, / Where locusts, ants, and lizards poorly thrive,— / […] / Were to an honest heart endurable, / Rather than such associates."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "800cb3a1-88cd-4d5d-88af-6df5d2063c70",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6b7055-2cb3-3ce7-8ed4-a1636b8a703c",
                                                "text": "In a country so vast as Canada, nothing but the railway could possibly save it from remaining a trackless, undeveloped wilderness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb5f9206-9c15-42a6-afc9-efab1791333b",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6b7055-2cb3-3ce7-8ed4-a1636b8a703c",
                                                "text": "\"You got two feet, Sethe, not four,\" he said, and right then a forest sprang up between them; trackless and quiet."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "422e377a-a38c-41a6-a04e-a0682676ecd7",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6b7055-2cb3-3ce7-8ed4-a1636b8a703c",
                                                "text": "At about this point, Seivarden and her two Amaats had made it into a cramped and dim access corridor behind the governor's residence. It had probably at one point been meant for servants to use to go unobtrusively back and forth, but hadn't been used in years; the floor was dusty and trackless."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "57778e1d-f647-49cc-8c36-b8bb62dad89d",
                                                "sense_id": "0e6b7055-2cb3-3ce7-8ed4-a1636b8a703c",
                                                "text": "The two structures remain in a remarkable state of preservation, despite finding themselves adrift and trackless in the County Down countryside, after the closure of the station and the line in the 1950s."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa6f4bfd-ebd5-3e95-a162-b1e988051fd3",
                                        "entry_id": "0119e4ed-481a-3b0f-83f4-1d6d11edc4ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Leaving no track or trace when moving; also, not following any track or path."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f44236ff-ee75-459c-baa3-f874c348b25a",
                                                "sense_id": "fa6f4bfd-ebd5-3e95-a162-b1e988051fd3",
                                                "text": "What was it that I loved so well about my childhood's home? / It was the wide and wave-lashed shore, the black rocks crowned with foam! / It was the sea-gull's flapping wing, all trackless in its flight, / Its screaming note, that welcomed on the fierce and stormy night!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dd67d33a-c796-3e92-abc7-02ea65685ee7",
                                        "entry_id": "0119e4ed-481a-3b0f-83f4-1d6d11edc4ed",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of a train, tram, etc.: not running on tracks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "decf0309-74f5-4dde-9cd5-a4f2aebbd8cf",
                                                "sense_id": "dd67d33a-c796-3e92-abc7-02ea65685ee7",
                                                "text": "a trackless trolley"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
